# Orders-to-PDF Script

The script in `backend/scripts/orders-to-pdf/` exports orders from api.infinitycolor.co (past week) into a single Persian PDF.

## How to run

- **Windows:** `backend\scripts\orders-to-pdf\run.bat`
- **Unix:** `./backend/scripts/orders-to-pdf/run.sh`

First run creates `.venv` and installs dependencies; then credentials are prompted and the PDF is generated.

## API

- **List orders:** `GET /api/orders` with:
  - `filters[Date][$gte]`, `filters[Date][$lte]` (ISO 8601)
  - `sort[0]=Date:desc`
  - `pagination[page]`, `pagination[pageSize]`
  - Full populate: user (user_info), contract (contract_transactions, payment_gateway), order_items (product_variation with product, CoverImage, product_variation_color/size/model, product_color, product_size, product_variation_model), delivery_address (shipping_city, shipping_province), shipping

## Credentials

- **Option A:** API Token – `INFINITY_API_TOKEN` or prompt. Used as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
- **Option B:** Phone + password – `INFINITY_PHONE` + `INFINITY_PASSWORD` or prompt. Script calls `POST /api/auth/login-with-password` and uses returned `jwt` as Bearer.

Optional: `INFINITY_API_BASE_URL` (default `https://api.infinitycolor.co`).

## Script args

- `--days N` (default 7)
- `--output FILE` (default orders.pdf)
- `--base-url URL`

## Key files

- `backend/scripts/orders-to-pdf/orders-to-pdf.py` – main script
- `backend/scripts/orders-to-pdf/requirements.txt` – requests, reportlab, arabic-reshaper, python-bidi
- `backend/scripts/orders-to-pdf/README.md` – user-facing docs
